    "description": "Infirmary, level 1 of 3: shell and fittings (what soldiers build first). Over budget: 448 blocks vs 285 (first build 379 vs 235). White plaster ward in a dark oak frame under a spruce gable roof, a red cross (bricks) in the front gable: six beds (three on each side, heads to the wall, a window over each), bedside tables, a hearth, herb barrels and shelves, a lean-to herb store; L2 adds the brewing stand and cauldron, candles, lanterns, flower boxes, a door canopy and the banner; L3 a herb garden, herb pots, more banners, a bench and a lantern post.",
    "changes": "Carlton: \"add a red cross\". A red cross of blocks (bricks: red wool is not builder-tested yet) on white plaster in the front gable overhang over the door, on every level; the L2 banner moved to the lean-to post so it does not cover it.",
